WEBVTT

00:07:29.139 --> 00:07:30.178
(Laughter)

00:07:30.202 --> 00:07:31.990
There's no running water,

00:07:32.014 --> 00:07:33.656
there's no trash pickup.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.264
At some point, the hallucinogens run out,

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.677
and you're stuck with a bunch
of wealthy white guys

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.003
in the dust in the desert.

00:07:40.027 --> 00:07:41.209
(Laughter)

00:07:41.233 --> 00:07:45.391
Which, to me, is sometimes
how social media feels in 2019.

00:07:45.415 --> 00:07:47.036
(Laughter)

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:51.423
A great, fun, hallucinatory place to visit
has become our home.

00:07:53.147 --> 00:07:54.551
And so,

00:07:54.575 --> 00:07:57.053
if we look at platforms
through the lens of spaces,

00:07:57.077 --> 00:07:58.664
we can then ask ourselves:

00:07:58.688 --> 00:08:02.807
Who knows how to structure spaces
for the public good?